#
# Tests that the liblog_unit_tests ctest entry leaves out.
#
# One test per line: the gtest name, a parity id and why it fails.  The
# parity id is a Linux system call from docs/specs/syscall-parity.md, or
# one of
#	abi:<name>	a row of docs/specs/abi-gap.md
#	tier0:<item>	something the tier-0 build does not have yet
#	env:<item>	a quirk of the FreeBSD dev VM, not of Android
#
# The tests of the files that system-tests.cmake does not build yet are
# here too, so that this file names every test that does not run.  The
# env:linker64-run rows apply only when the suite runs as
# "linker64 liblog-unit-tests", which run-gtest-suite.sh does when it cannot
# make the jail.
#
# Tests that call GTEST_SKIP() on FreeBSD are not listed here.

liblog.__android_log_btwrite__android_logger_list_read  tier0:toybox  As root the test runs grep on /proc/net/unix to see the logdw socket: tier 0 has no toybox, and aprocfs has no /proc/net/unix. The rest of the test passes (m: run as the shell user).
